{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1379907-night-horrors-mythic-foes","id":1379907,"title":"Night Horrors, Mythic Foes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-09T15:49:42-07:00","id":1379907,"title":"Night Horrors, Mythic Foes","content":"So once upon a time I read Night Horrors, Conquering Heroes... &amp; I was a little disappointed.<br /> Don't get me wrong, it was great on multiple levels, I loved the introduction of the Insatiables, &amp; it was good to see more variation with the Heroes. But, with a several entries I got a bit of a feeling of sameness.<br /> I don't know if anyone else felt this, but I got the idea into my head to start building a list of various ideas for entries of a second Beast the Primordial Night Horrors book, which I have titled &quot;Mythic Foes&quot;.<br /> This thread is basically me sharing these ideas with the community.<br /> Note, some of them are very threadbare.<br /> <br /> This &quot;book&quot; has been divided up into three chapters which are further divided.<br /> <br /> Chapter 1: Halfway Sleeping/In the Dream<br /> This chapter covers Begotten, Heroes, Insatiable, &amp; other creatures firmly rooted in the Primordial Dream. Also certain phenomenon of the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> Chapter 2: Halfway Waking/In the Waking World<br /> This chapter covers hunters &amp; other stuff of the material world that has been touched by the Primordial Dream in one way or another.<br /> <br /> Chapter 3: Outside the Dream/Other Monsters<br /> Finally, this chapter covers creatures from other gamelines which have developed a connection of some sort to the Primordial Dream.<br /> I really feel Night Horrors, Conquering Heroes should have had something like this last chapter. Intellectually, I know what it didn't but it still bothers me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":"04-09-2020, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:07:37-07:00","id":1379911,"title":"","content":"Chapter 1<br /> Begotten<br /> \u2022 A Begotten with a Sorrow instead of a Horror.<br /> \u2022 Ancient Horror/Recurrent Soul Begotten.<br /> \u2022 Demon-possessed Begotten.<br /> \u2022 A Distorted Begotten (suffers from the Geryo disease).<br /> \u2022 Multi-Headed Begotten.<br /> \u2022 Sorcerer Incarnate.<br /> \u2022 A self-proclaimed high priest of the Dark Mother. Skilled in Obascus Rites.<br /> \u2022 Tiny Terror Beast Rampant.<br /> \u2022 Twin-Souled Begotten.<br /> \u2022 An Unfettered that lives far to the north, where the snow never melts. It is a persistent nightmare of the local Inuits.<br /> \u2022 A Begotten that didn't get devoured, rather they chose to become a Begotten.<br /> \u2022 A Begotten that is the ultimate expression of individual over society.<br /> \u2022 A Beast Incarnate that has acquired a small &quot;brood&quot; of Beasts Rampant to serve it.<br /> \u2022 A Begotten whose &quot;Horror&quot; was born in the Bright Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:12:35-07:00","id":1379918,"title":"","content":"Chapter 1<br /> Heroes<br /> \u2022 Ancient Horror/Recurrent Soul Hero.<br /> \u2022 Herald of a Primordial Cult turned Hero.<br /> \u2022 Monster Tamer Hero.<br /> \u2022 Obsessively glory-seeking Hero.<br /> \u2022 A Regnans or Hero Ascendant.<br /> \u2022 A Hero that is an expression of society over individual.<br /> \u2022 A sort of reverse Hero called a Prophet that's connected to the Bright Dream not the Primordial Dream.<br /> \u2022 #1 Hero with Lineage &amp; Longing.<br /> \u2022 #2 Hero with Lineage &amp; Longing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:21:00-07:00","id":1379923,"title":"","content":"Where I got this fanmade stuff from: <br /> Ancient Horror, Recurrent Soul, Multi-Headed, Twin-Souled, Tiny Terror are all fanmade Beast the Primordial Merits found on this site, most on the Beast fan-made Merits thread.<br /> I'm not really sure what the difference between the Ancient Horror Merit &amp; the Recurrent Soul Merit is.<br /> Information on the reverse-Heroes called Prophets can be found on another thread, along with the information about Hero Lineages &amp; Longings.<br /> The Monster Tamer Hero is a variation on the Hero that was conjured yet another thread on this site.<br /> The rest of the fanmade stuff, I can't remember where I got it from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:23:50-07:00","id":1379924,"title":"","content":"Chapter 1<br /> Insatiables<br /> \u2022 An Insatiable Incarnate.<br /> \u2022 The Insatiable who birthed the Insatiable-Blooded (this is a strain of demon-blooded that I haven't posted yet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:33:26-07:00","id":1379927,"title":"","content":"Chapter 1<br /> Other Inhabitants of the Dream<br /> \u2022 Alebrije.<br /> \u2022 Apparently normal people who each build a Chamber in the Primordial Dream for themselves.<br /> \u2022 Desolation: a vast abandoned Lair that draws sleeping souls to feed it, &amp; consumes normal Laird to grow. Inspired by the Empty City of the Fear Mythos.<br /> \u2022 Fauna of the Primordial Dream (Nemeans, etc.).<br /> \u2022 A few lesser Protogenoi.<br /> \u2022 Flora of the Primordial Dream (Blind Panic, Immigrant-Job-Theft Dandelions, Red-Scare Kudzu, etc.).<br /> \u2022 A greater Protogenoi.<br /> \u2022 The Mythophagi.<br /> \u2022 A Night-Gaunt.<br /> \u2022 A pair of Night Terrors.<br /> \u2022 A predatory monster that moves through the Primordial Dream, hunting down Horrors to kill &amp; devour.<br /> \u2022 A rogue Horrorspawn.<br /> \u2022 A Sorrow.<br /> \u2022 A creature of the Bright Dream that has wandered into the Primordial Dream.<br /> A ship crewed by ephemeral entities that voyages through the Primordial Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:38:42-07:00","id":1379931,"title":"","content":"Chapter 1<br /> Miscellaneous<br /> \u2022 A location that overlaps with the Primordial Dream.<br /> \u2022 A Mythic Item that leaves destruction in its wake.<br /> \u2022 The Nightmare Maelstrom.<br /> \u2022 The remnants of an Unchained that went to the Dark Mother to hide from the God-Machine &amp; now rests in its own little corner of the Primordial Dream. This act created the Automata Family.<br /> \u2022 A disease that affects Begotten, causing their Horror to leak into their physical form.<br /> \u2022 A disease that causes feeding Begotten to infect those they feed off with little bits of their Horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:40:53-07:00","id":1379932,"title":"","content":"To my knowledge, everything from the previous two posts is either my own creation, or comes from the thread &quot;Nightmares &amp; Dreamscapes: Incursions from the Primordial Dream&quot;.<br /> I apologize if I am incorrect in this regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:50:25-07:00","id":1379937,"title":"","content":"Chapter 2<br /> Hunters<br /> \u2022 An experienced Knight of the Bloody Chalice.<br /> \u2022 A newly recruited Knight of the Bloody Chalice.<br /> \u2022 The current King of the Bloody Chalice (who I imagine as a woman).<br /> \u2022 An Insatiable-Blooded that is of the modern American faction.<br /> \u2022 An Insatiable-Blooded that is of the traditional African faction.<br /> \u2022 A member of the Merrick Institute who is suffering from a severe psychotic break.<br /> \u2022 A member of the Burya Storozh who is also in the Russian Mafiya.<br /> \u2022 A member of the Cheiron Group whose newest implant enables them to enter the Primordial Dream &amp; physically extract stuff.<br /> \u2022 A member of Malleus Maleficarum who means to exorcise the demons known as Begotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":". 07-28-2020, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:52:26-07:00","id":1379939,"title":"","content":"Chapter 2<br /> Non-Humans<br /> \u2022 A caliban.<br /> \u2022 Flora/fauna that has been touched by the Primordial Dream, going through a sort of mini-Devouring of their own.<br /> \u2022 The ghost of a human that has become a Begotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:56:29-07:00","id":1379941,"title":"","content":"Chapter 2<br /> Others<br /> \u2022 A Dark Lord.<br /> \u2022 Formidolosii.<br /> \u2022 The Primordial Mutation.<br /> \u2022 Primordial Sorcerer (Dark Sage, Primeval Necromancer, Primeval Shaman, Speaker of Curses, etc.).<br /> \u2022 Primordial Witch.<br /> \u2022 Terror Carriers.<br /> \u2022 A psychic(?) of awesome might. They drag masses of people into the Primordial Dream every time they go to sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:00:43-07:00","id":1379945,"title":"","content":"So far, everything above is: <br /> A) Official material.<br /> B) Can be found somewhere on this site.<br /> C) Is of my own invention.<br /> Felt like I needed to establish that.<br /> <br /> Groups that I have not covered so far in this Chapter are: Hero-Blooded; Llannerch Athrawon; Navio de Tolos; Nightmare Network; the Reckoning; Yam VeNahar Factories; Yuri's Group","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":". 10-25-2020, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:09:47-07:00","id":1379949,"title":"","content":"Chapter 3<br /> Changeling<br /> \u2022 An Autumn Court changeling.<br /> \u2022 An oneiromantic changeling that has started dipping into the Primordial Dream &amp; not the Skein (changeling dreamscape).<br /> \u2022 A hobgoblin who goes out of its way to be the perfect friend to broods of Begotten. When they are offered kinship bonds/to join the brood accepts, &amp; then starts poisoning the broods against themselves.<br /> \u2022 A True Fae that has, somehow, managed to make connections between its domain &amp; the Primordial Dream. The changelings that escape from it are all bound to the Primordial Dream.<br /> \u2022 A member of the Scarecrow Ministry who feels that they must outdo all the Begotten in the area, &amp; become the Apex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:11:52-07:00","id":1379951,"title":"","content":"Chapter 3<br /> Mage<br /> \u2022 A Horror that was given birth, not by the Dark Mother &amp; the Primordial Dream, but by the Abyss.<br /> \u2022 A mage Legacy that was founded on controlling the Primordial Dream.<br /> \u2022 One of the Fangs of Mara, who knows of the Primordial Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:16:06-07:00","id":1379953,"title":"","content":"Chapter 3<br /> Mummy<br /> \u2022 A mummy that believes that they should resurrect the Nameless Empire, &amp; that the secrets to do so lie within the Primordial Dream.<br /> \u2022 A memory of the Nameless Empire that tears through the Astral Realms, dipping in &amp; out of the Primordial Dream in its travels.<br /> \u2022 A Judge that hides in the Primordial Dream from some ancient foe. How the Judge got into the Dream in the first place is a mystery, but the Dark Mother isn't throwing it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:19:49-07:00","id":1379958,"title":"","content":"Chapter 3<br /> Vampire<br /> \u2022 A vampire Bloodline born from the worship of the Dark Mother.<br /> \u2022 A Nosferatu whose use of Nightmare (as a result of a taste for Begotten blood) has warped to create physical manifestations of people's fears.<br /> \u2022 A Bloodline connected to the Circle of the Crone that has developed a Discipline to manipulate the Primordial Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:29:31-07:00","id":1379962,"title":"","content":"Chapter 3<br /> Werewolf<br /> \u2022 A Begotten who got infected by a Beshilu looking to make itself a hybrid. The resulting creature is a monster resembling a cross between an oversized, humanoid rat &amp; whatever the Begotten's Horror was. It has become possessed by the idea of fear as a disease &amp; intends to make this &quot;fear plague&quot;. It also likes teaching &quot;lessons&quot;, but only ones that make sense to its warped mind.<br /> \u2022 The Leopard/Tiger Host (information on this can be found on the thread &quot;Possible Host Concepts?&quot;).<br /> \u2022 A Geryo.<br /> \u2022 A vicious anshega who has learnt how to draw upon the Primordial Dream for power.<br /> \u2022 A Leopard Man loyal to the Insatiable-Blooded Insatiable.<br /> \u2022 A small-town werewolf belonging to the Lodge of the Screaming Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:34:21-07:00","id":1379963,"title":"","content":"Chapter 3<br /> The Rest<br /> \u2022 A mysterious creature which can turn Begotten back into humans, for a price. Oh, &amp; the souls needed for such a task, it steals from innocent victims.<br /> \u2022 An angel that has been tasked, by the God-Machine, to find some way to affect the Begotten &amp; other things of the Primordial Dream.<br /> \u2022 A Noble (Princess: The Hopeful).<br /> \u2022 A Promethean that was made by a Begotten.<br /> \u2022 A Sin-Eater that has seen too many ghosts of the victims of the Begotten. Now they hunt Begotten in revenge for these hurting dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:36:27-07:00","id":1379965,"title":"","content":"I've got some more to post on this thread. Plus, I feel like Chapter 3 is incomplete without anything from Deviant: The Renegades. But for now this is where I'm going to stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T20:46:16-07:00","id":1380015,"title":"","content":"I've got found two more things to go on this thread. This first one, would probably go into Chapter 1: <br /> <br /> A thing. Every day it has a new Hunger &amp; a new Horror. It goes around doing its best to teach people lessons, Begotten style. But there's no sanity or coherence behind it &amp; so the &quot;students&quot; just get damaged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T20:54:14-07:00","id":1380017,"title":"","content":"The second is something I had to think about the structure of it (as opposed to the thing in the previous post). It is my attempt at making an antagonistic Primordial Cult, which I really wanted to do ever since I first started coming up with entries for Night Horrors, Mythic Foes, &amp; I feel like it came out really good.<br /> <br /> Cirque du R\u00eaver<br /> A traveling circus &amp; hanger-ons that has a dark secret.<br /> Long ago (maybe) there was a Begotten with a Primordial Cult. In time the Begotten was killed by a Hero, &amp; in the wake of this event the cultists found themselves without purpose &amp; not regressing back into non-Primordial Cultist people.<br /> At some point they found former members of another Primordial Cult &amp; absorbed them for want of a better word. Still looking for a purpose, they repeated this several times before finding a Begotten they could serve, &amp; all was well. Until the Begotten died.<br /> After the fifth Begotten died, the ringleaders of this disturbing patchwork of Primordial Cults came together to figure out how to properly solve their problem. And they came upon a solution.<br /> Taking the name Cirque du R\u00eaver, they fashioned themselves into a traveling circus &amp; began moving across the land in search of Begotten. Not to serve, oh no they had tried that &amp; it always ended in failure, but to capture so that they could bask in the glory of their gods whenever they needed to.<br /> Haven't you heard? The circus is in town!<br /> <br /> The name is French (I think) for Circus of Dream, which might not be grammatically correct, but a bit of incorrect grammer in the name feels right for the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}